Package: ggplasmidZY
Title: Plasmid-First Linear and Circular Maps with ggplot2
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R: c(
    person("Zhong", "Yang", role = c("aut", "cre"), email = "yzhong005@e.ntu.edu.sg")
  )
Author: Zhong Yang
Maintainer: Zhong Yang <yzhong005@e.ntu.edu.sg>
Description: Generate publication-quality genetic maps, with particular
    suitability for plasmids and bacteriophages. Built entirely within the
    ggplot2 framework, ggplasmidZY supports both circular and linear plotting of
    annotated genetic features. Its intelligent label-placement algorithm
    automatically minimizes label overlap, making it effective for densely
    annotated multidrug-resistant plasmids containing numerous resistance genes,
    mobile genetic elements, and other labeled features. It can also plot
    circular or linear bacteriophage genome maps, including a terminal marker
    option for linear phage genomes. The package provides a curated catalogue of
    color palettes for genetic features and labels, and supports palettes from
    ggsci.
